          "Address the 18.3% college attainment rate as a workforce development opportunity, not an abstract education issue — connect K-12 education, community college access, and career pathways to specific jobs that pay above minimum wage and allow households to build economic stability.",
          "Monitor rural healthcare access and property tax burden as the two most likely early warning indicators of constituent dissatisfaction — if these conditions deteriorate for working-class households, the 99% result becomes a vulnerability rather than a strength."
