          "Engage the multiracial working-class coalition directly: the 61.64% white, 25.01% Black, and 6.83% Hispanic breakdown at a 68% Democratic margin means white working-class voters are part of the winning coalition, not opposition. Frame economic policy as lifting all working families together rather than as identity-group allocation, which would fracture the coalition that just voted Democratic.",
          "Recognize that this is a young district with different values and concerns than traditional Democratic constituencies: the 26.0 median age means a constituency shaped by housing unaffordability, student debt, climate anxiety, and skepticism of institutional stability — not the legacy Democratic issues of union organizing or retiree security. Policy and messaging must reflect what actually concerns people who are 26, not what concerned their parents.",
