          "This district delivered 84% of its vote to the Republican candidate in 2024, representing a supermajority hold that requires no persuasion strategy—only retention. The demographic and economic profile reveals why: a population that is 88.9% white, median age 43.2, with college education at just 15.5% and median household income at $55,528. This is a working-and middle-class constituency anchored in stable, non-college careers, likely including manufacturing, construction, skilled trades, and service sectors. The 24.4% renter rate signals economic vulnerability among renters and property owners alike, making cost-of-living pressures a lived daily reality. The strength of the incumbent's 84% margin means the campaign is about consolidation and preventing defection, not persuading Democratic voters.",
