          "Do not assume the 84% is a floor: this is a supermajority result, but it is built on an economically fragile working-class constituency under material pressure; if an incumbent takes the margin for granted and does not actively address working-class economic concerns, a credible challenger with a concrete economic message could reduce the margin significantly in the next cycle."
