          "Defend public education and education funding specifically: with 37.2% college education, this district contains parents with direct stakes in K-12 education quality and higher education affordability—areas where Republican messaging has lost ground with college-educated suburbanites. A clear, affirmative agenda on education quality and workforce development neutralizes a Democratic opening.",
          "Monitor the 32% Democratic base for signs of activation: the college-educated suburban portion of TN-HD-45 is the demographic cohort most likely to support a high-quality Democratic challenger if one emerges. Ignoring or dismissing the opposition's presence is a strategic error; engagement and specific outreach to college-educated voters on economic and quality-of-life concerns are necessary to prevent a competitive race.",
          "Avoid ideological positioning that alienates college-educated voters: this constituency is less responsive to cultural conservatism and more responsive to fiscal competence, local governance effectiveness, and whether government is solving real problems. Any messaging that prioritizes ideological purity over constituent service will find purchase among the 32% and risk eroding the 68%."
