          { name: "Overlooking Economic Anxiety Among Renters and Service-Sector Workers", tag: "avoid", why: "While TN-HD-53's 44% college education and $76,954 income appear relatively stable, the 49.8% renter rate and 32.8 median age signal a constituency in economic transition — many renters are young professionals building careers, others are service-sector workers for whom $76,954 household income represents two-worker stability rather than individual security. If Powell's representation defaults to speaking primarily to the college-educated professional class and neglects the material cost-of-living concerns of renters and service workers, that neglect will activate opposition among a constituency whose material conditions are precarious despite aggregate income statistics." }
