          "Lead on the issues that matter to educated urban professionals aged 31 with $98K household income: education funding and school quality, housing affordability and zoning reform, public transit and walkability, environmental sustainability, and criminal justice reform. These are not abstract values but material governance concerns for the district's primary constituency.",
          "Recognize the 49.2% renter rate as a sign of demographic transience: younger professionals without deep community roots may not have inherited partisan loyalty and will evaluate representation on specific policy delivery and constituent responsiveness rather than party default. Build durable connection through visible effectiveness on district priorities, not partisan assumption.",
          "Monitor for potential challenger emergence from within the Democratic coalition itself: in an unopposed district, a primary challenger from a more ideologically aligned or identity-representative candidate could emerge if the incumbent appears insufficiently responsive to progressive urban priorities or constituent service expectations. Maintain credibility on the left by regular delivery on stated priorities."
