          "Address rural service decline and housing affordability as primary quality-of-life issues: a district with 28.1% renters, $61,904 median income, and only 18.2% college attainment is likely experiencing rising housing costs relative to stagnant wages, and rural infrastructure decline in healthcare, broadband, and local services; messaging that centers these material concerns will resonate more effectively than messaging that assumes inherited partisan loyalty."
