          { name: "Social or Cultural Messaging Over Governance Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "A constituency of affluent, college-educated professionals and business owners evaluates primarily on fiscal discipline, education investment, and quality-of-life outcomes — not on social or cultural positioning. An incumbent who substitutes social messaging or partisan identity appeals for specific legislative accomplishments on the issues this demographic actually cares about (taxes, schools, infrastructure, economic competitiveness) will find that messaging ineffective and potentially alienating to the college-educated swing voters who represent the electoral volatility in this district." }
