          "Lead with specific property tax and education funding answers: in an affluent district where homeowners have significant wealth in residential property and parents evaluate schools on outcomes, Republican durability depends on demonstrating that the party delivers on these core suburban concerns rather than defaulting to culture-war messaging.",
          "Monitor Democratic growth in the 31% — particularly among college-educated women and professionals in healthcare, education, and technology sectors — as an early indicator of whether the current 69% is sustainable or whether affluent suburban realignment is taking hold in TN-HD-65.",
          "Engage the renter 20.4% as an often-overlooked constituency: while homeowners dominate, one in five households rents, and rental affordability in an affluent district reflects younger professionals and service workers who may feel economically excluded from the district's prosperity — concrete housing and cost-of-living policy can address this constituency's concerns."
