          "Treat 55% as a narrow plurality, not a durable majority: a 10-point margin in a district with the youngest median age among comparable urban seats is not a safe floor; it reflects current consolidation of the white base and split or low minority turnout—both conditions that can change if an opponent offers credible engagement on minority communities' economic and safety concerns.",
