          "Engage young adult economic mobility directly: the 30.8 median age signals a constituency evaluating on education access, job training, wage growth, and whether government is creating pathways to economic security — not inherited partisan loyalty — and specific legislative focus on workforce development and vocational education is essential to retaining support among this demographic.",
          "Build visible constituent relationships with neighborhood institutions, community organizations, and faith leaders: unopposed status creates the risk that an incumbent becomes invisible in constituent life, allowing future challengers to define the narrative — active engagement in community meetings, problem-solving on individual constituent issues, and visible partnership with neighborhood institutions is the foundation of durable support.",
