          "Address housing affordability and renter concerns directly: the 31.4% renter rate combined with $89,188 median income signals young professionals and dual-income households evaluating whether housing costs are sustainable and whether zoning/development policy supports residential options at middle-class price points. This is a material economic issue, not a secondary concern.",
          "Engage the college-educated, suburban-professional constituency on tax structure and service delivery: at this income level with high education and professional employment, voters evaluate government on whether it delivers infrastructure, services, and accountability — not on abstract ideology. Speak specifically about what your budget priorities accomplish for this district, not partisan rhetoric.",
