          "Monitor demographic drift carefully: a district at 71.29% white with 82.9% homeownership is secure today but not automatically secure in five cycles if Hispanic, Asian, or younger renter households grow as a share of the population; early engagement with demographic minorities and younger adults prevents the emergence of an opposition alternative that consolidates around perceived neglect.",
          "Engage the college-educated professional constituency (38.9%) with specificity on issues where affluent, educated voters have shown capacity to swing: public education quality and funding, higher education affordability, healthcare access and cost control, environmental stewardship — these are not Democratic issues but issues where educated constituencies evaluate based on outcomes rather than party label.",
          "Do not treat a 75-25 margin as permission to govern for the top quartile alone; a representative who appears to serve only the most affluent households and ignores working families, renters, or racial minorities in the district creates a perception vulnerability that can crystallize opposition in a future cycle when a credible alternative emerges."
