          "Engage the 31.7% renter population and younger households on housing affordability and economic opportunity: renters vote differently than homeowners and are more price-sensitive to housing costs and employment stability—addressing entry-level wage stagnation and housing supply credibly converts this constituency from passive opposition into active support and increases durability of the seat.",
          "Develop specific, credible answers to cost-of-living pressure across healthcare, education, and services: the 28.2% college attainment and middle-income profile indicate a constituency that evaluates on whether government is delivering concrete improvement in their economic security, not on partisan messaging—candidates who offer specific remedies outperform those who rely on party brand.",
          "Avoid treating 75% as a safe majority: a supermajority built on conditional economic satisfaction, not ideological alignment or deep partisan identification, is vulnerable to a credible challenger offering better economic outcomes—any incumbent who consolidates the existing coalition without actively addressing the base's cost-of-living concerns risks a surprise closer race in the next cycle."
