          "Engage the 25.4% renter minority—disproportionately younger and Hispanic—with concrete governance on housing affordability and wage access; treating them as a permanent Democratic constituency forfeits the opportunity to demonstrate that competent Republican governance serves all constituents, and it leaves an opening for Democratic recruitment of a growing demographic bloc.",
          "Protect property tax structure and rural service delivery as baseline governance commitments; the 75% homeowner base is evaluating whether their elected official is defending their property interests and maintaining the service infrastructure that supports rural communities—routine but essential governance that a supermajority makes possible.",
          "Do not mistake 77% supermajority for a mandate to govern by values alone; use the political safety to deliver substantive policy on healthcare, infrastructure, and economic development that a 45-year-old homeowner majority actually cares about more than cultural messaging."
