          "Actively engage the 31.6% renter segment and younger professionals with economic opportunity messaging: housing affordability, wage growth, and childcare access are the concerns most likely to drive the 36% opposition and most amenable to specific policy remedies that differentiate the incumbent from generic Republican positioning. The absence of a substantial crossover demographic means this segment cannot be written off — their mobilization or demobilization directly determines the margin.",
          "Build sufficient constituent relationship depth to weather polarization: a 64% margin in a deeply divided environment is not self-sustaining if the incumbent is perceived as distant or unresponsive. Town halls, constituent service capacity, and visible engagement on local issues create the personal credibility that allows a representative to hold an upper-middle-class constituency even when partisan environments shift.",
          "Do not treat the 64% as a safe majority in a polarized state: Tennessee's recent Republican acceleration makes this margin feel stable, but it is built on active retention of an educated, income-secure, and economically attentive constituency. Any incumbent who campaigns this seat as though 64% is a comfortable floor rather than actively maintained will be vulnerable to a credible challenger who addresses the 36% opposition's actual concerns with specificity."
