          "Monitor Democratic recruitment and challenger positioning closely — the 38% is large enough and educated enough that a credible challenger with professional credentials and a business-friendly but socially moderate platform could make this genuinely competitive. The seat's security rests on continuous engagement with the educated middle-class constituency, not on demographic inevitability.",
          "Avoid culture-war positioning that alienates the college-educated professional minority within the Republican coalition; these voters are persuadable toward Democratic challengers if they perceive the Republican incumbent as ideologically rigid on social issues while inattentive to their economic concerns.",
          "Invest in constituent service infrastructure and local visibility among the 43.8% college-educated population — this demographic cohort evaluates politicians on competence and responsiveness to their specific needs rather than inherited partisan loyalty, making continuous engagement the difference between a 62% that holds and one that erodes."
