          { name: "Taking the Unopposed 2022 Victory as Durable Proof of Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "The absence of a Republican opponent in 2022 does not establish that TN SD-11 is a structurally Democratic seat — it establishes only that the current incumbent deterred opposition in that cycle. Given the district's demographic conservatism (high income, high homeownership, mature age, college-educated but not progressive-identified), any Republican challenger who offers homeowner tax protection, education funding specificity, and fiscal responsibility framing will find this a genuinely competitive race. The seat's fundamentals are persuadable; the 2022 unopposed result is not evidence of partisan lock but of current incumbent credibility." }
