          { name: "Taking Low-Education, Low-Income Constituency Loyalty for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "Working-class, low-college-attainment constituencies with constrained incomes have demonstrated across multiple states and cycles that they will switch partisan preference when a credible alternative offers material economic improvement — they are not ideologically locked into either party. At $53,081 income and 15.4% college attainment, TN-SD-12 fits the profile of constituencies that swung heavily toward Donald Trump in 2016 and 2020 based on economic messaging, but that have also swung toward Democratic candidates offering healthcare expansion or wage-growth policies. An incumbent who assumes this constituency's loyalty is safe without delivering on economic performance is misreading the political reality of working-class voter behavior." }
