          "Consolidate credibility on workforce development and wage-growth pathways: the 25.9% college-attainment rate and 34.6-year median age signal a working-age constituency constrained by educational access and wage stagnation; specific legislative action on community college funding, apprenticeship programs, and employer partnerships is more persuasive than partisan messaging.",
          "Do not treat 68% as a safe majority: the combination of 37.5% renters, 25.9% college attainment, and a 34.6-year median age creates a constituency that evaluates on economic delivery rather than partisan loyalty; any incumbent who consolidates only the homeowner base and ignores working-age renters' cost-of-living concerns will find the margin more vulnerable in a competitive cycle than current partisan alignment suggests.",
