          "Address younger adult economic mobility explicitly: at 34.1 median age with 28.3% college attainment and 55.2% renting, this district includes significant populations of young adults without four-year degrees who face constrained job markets and housing costs; workforce development, vocational training access, and affordable housing are not boutique issues here — they are central to whether young people stay in Nashville.",
          "Avoid treating the 80% as permission to shift focus away from constituent service — supermajorities in working-class districts are brittle when material conditions stagnate; the vulnerability is not to Republican persuasion but to a primary challenger who argues the incumbent has not effectively leveraged Democratic control to improve economic security for working families."
